\textit{Linear negation} is defined by the following function over formulae.
\begin{gather*}
\co{\cunit} = \cunit
\qquad
\co{\co{\alpha}} = \alpha
\qquad
\co{ P \tensor Q } = \co{P} \cpar \co{Q}
\qquad
\co{ P \cpar Q } = \co{P} \tensor \co{Q}
\qquad
\co{P \cseq Q} = \co{P} \cseq \co{Q}
\qquad
\co{\nabla x. P} = \nabla x. \co{P}
\end{gather*}
\textit{Linear implication}, written $P \multimap Q$, is defined as $\co{P} \cpar Q$.

\begin{gather*}
\co{\cunit} = \cunit
\qquad
\co{\co{\alpha}} = \alpha
\qquad
\co{ P \tensor Q } = \co{P} \cpar \co{Q}
\qquad
\co{ P \cpar Q } = \co{P} \tensor \co{Q}
\qquad
\co{P \cseq Q} = \co{P} \cseq \co{Q}
\qquad
\co{\nabla x. P} = \nabla x. \co{P}
\end{gather*}

